A||||5||Seanh||Need Help with Winter beater (85 Ford Bronco 5.0 V8)||||11||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-11-2000||09:19 PM||||Well, it snowed like crazy today. 6-7 inches so far, and no cars, except my Bronco made it out of the drive way (you go up the drive way from our grage). First time I used 4 wheel drive all year. Anyway, my problems. The car starts very hard all the time. I suspect carb problems since the carb is covered with oil/gas and the air filter is black. I would like to rebuild it and get her running good. It gets at most 9 mpg highway. Also, has 266K on it, these problems can be excepted. The one other problem I have is. The crank case ventalation hole on the valve cover is shooting oil. I have the cap on, but there is a hose going from the cap to the air filter housing, I took it off because it was clogging up the air filter almost monthly. It sprays oil out of it in a misty steam all the time. What the heck do I do? There is a filter inside the air cleaner housing that filters the hose, but it gets clogged too. My father (the real owner of the truck) thinks it has alot of blow by, and adds oil all the time because he cant find any on the dipstick. Could this be the result from over filling maybe? I agree, there is not much oil at all on the stick, way below the add line. Also, there is some black smoke out the tail pipes on start up, what does this mean? What all should I do to get this truck running smoothly. I forgot to say that it will idel okay somtimes, but others it dies and is very hard to start up again. I havent replaced plugs, wires, cap, or rotor for a long time, so I am sure that is a good place to start. I am sure it needs to be timed also. A while back the belts needed replacing and the mechanic asked if we wanted him to replace the belt that runs the emmission control thingy, and he also said while being illegal, it wouldnt hurt the truck at all. So we didnt replace it. I am wonding if this may be causing problems? Thanks<P>Sorry, my bad, it is a 5.7L, not 5.0<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">     <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I><p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||Seanh||11-11-2000||09:26 PM||||Forgot to say that the darn battery alway is discharged. In warm weather it will hold a charge for a couple monthes, but it wouldnt today. I think it might be from the long starting time to get it running, but I am not sure. I am also thinking a short, but I dont know how to check for one. Could I put an amp meter on the battery when the truck is sitting? There are not blown fuses. I checked the voltage today when the truck wouldnt even click the starter, 11.87 volts. Again when the battery just got off a charger, 12.4 volts. I started it and checked, 13.8 volts with nothing on, 13.4 with heater on full. I also noticed tonight that when the truck was idle (with my foot on gas to keep it running) and I shut off the headlights, the heater started blowing alot more then with headlights on. Whats up? Bad alternator? The battery is just over a year old. Thanks again.<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-11-2000||10:42 PM||||If the truck is full size and has a V-8 in it , like maybe a 351 or a 351 modified 400, Pull the valve covers and take a screw driver and scoop the guck out of the rear oil return holes on the cylinder head. If it has a lot of blow-by the oil that is traped on top of the head will find a way out, goes in to the air cleaner the right side, and the pvc valve on the left. If your dad checks the oil after it runs, like when he gets gas, the oil on top has no waay to get back to the pan quick.After you do this and put on new valve cover gaskets, get new filters for the air cleaner and clean, clean, and clean again the pvc line to the base of the carb, and install new pvc valve.<BR>The hard starting with a full charge in the battery sounds like a new starter is required!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-11-2000||10:48 PM||||Thanks. Should have said that before but it also has a new starter also. It froze up and need one. It did the same thing before this and after the new one. I think it is a bad carb, not closing the butterfly and flooding the engine. It starts quick a great if it sits overnight. I will try that tomarrow. Thanks||||reg||1
